  "_readme": [
    "Folded (lowercased, unaccented) given name -> category, for names that",
    "scripts/build-name-pool.js pulls out of the SSA data. Category is an",
    "ORGANISATIONAL LABEL - it groups the admin Name Pool tab and gives a life",
    "its cultural texture. It is NOT a selection weight: real region_frequency",
    "counts carry commonality now.",
    "",
    "Only names that differ from mainstream American naming stock are listed.",
    "Anything absent defaults to \"anglo\", which is the right label for the bulk",
    "of the SSA top-N and is reported as a count, not a warning. Naturalised",
    "biblical names (David, Sarah, Noah, Rachel) are anglo on purpose - the",
    "pool's hebrew entries (Eitan, Noam, Shoshana, Tamar) show what that label",
    "is reserved for.",
    "",
    "Keys beginning with an underscore are ignored by the builder."
  ],
